      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "First, immediately run cold water over the burn for several minutes to cool it down and prevent further injury. Do not apply butter, lotion, or try to pop any blister; these actions can worsen the condition. Use a sterile burn dressing and seek medical attention right away. If the area is still red and blistering, you may also need to change bandages and follow up with a doctor. It's important to keep the burn clean and covered to aid in healing and prevent infection.",
